postvec — license index
=======================

This repository holds two products with different terms. This file says which
license covers which directory; the full texts are where the table points.

  Path                              License        Text
  --------------------------------  -------------  --------------------------
  postvec/                          PostgreSQL     below, and postvec/LICENSE
  postvec-cli/                      PostgreSQL     below
  packaging/postvec/                PostgreSQL     below
  engine/                           PostgreSQL     below
  shared/                           PostgreSQL     below
  providers/                        PostgreSQL     below
  proto/                            PostgreSQL     below
  registry/schema/                  PostgreSQL     below
  docs/                             PostgreSQL     below
  postvec-server/                   BUSL-1.1       postvec-server/LICENSE

The PostgreSQL License below therefore covers everything published as a
postvec release artifact — the extension, the `postvec` command, their
packaging, and the inference engine embedded mode links into the database
process. That grant is unconditional: it does not depend on which mode you run
postvec in, on how much traffic you serve, or on whether you charge for what
you build with it.

`postvec-server/` is a separate program — a standalone inference node for
postvec's remote mode — under the Business Source License 1.1
(source-available; production use by an organization needs a commercial
license; see postvec-server/LICENSE). It links the PostgreSQL-licensed crates
above and does not change their terms.

Third-party components redistributed alongside postvec keep their own
licenses; see NOTICE.


